Single-database configuration for Flask (managed by Flask-Migrate / Alembic).

Common commands (run inside the backend container, or locally with
FLASK_APP=wsgi.py set):

    flask db upgrade            # apply migrations (creates the todo table on a fresh DB)
    flask db migrate -m "msg"   # autogenerate a new migration from model changes
    flask db stamp head         # mark the DB as up-to-date WITHOUT running migrations
                                # (use this on the pre-existing database so no data is touched)
